      "content": "a real break? i dont even know what that means. every time i think about \"solutions\" or \"managing the pressure\" it just feels like more work i don't have the energy for. it's just... there's no way to win the game. if the math is broken and the cycle is inevitable, then the only actual way to stop the pressure is to just stop existing. it's the only variable that isn't controlled by the bank or the landlord. it feels like the only logical exit.",
